import { site } from '@/config/site';
const mail = site.contactEmail;
---
<p>This policy explains what happens to the information you give Encore through this website. Right now that means one thing: the email address you enter to join the early-access waitlist.</p>

<h2>Who is responsible for your data</h2>
<p>Encore is responsible for the personal data collected on this website. You can reach us about anything in this policy at <a href={`mailto:${mail}`}>{mail}</a>.</p>

<h2>What we collect</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Your email address</strong>, when you join the waitlist.</li>
  <li><strong>The date and time</strong> you joined.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not ask for your name, phone number or location, and this website does not use advertising or analytics cookies.</p>

<h2>Why we collect it</h2>
<p>We use your email address only to tell you about Encore: when early access opens, and important news about the launch. We will never sell it or share it with anyone for their own marketing.</p>
<p>We process it because you asked to join the waitlist and gave us your consent. You can withdraw that consent at any time.</p>

<h2>Where it is stored</h2>
<p>Waitlist addresses are stored in a PostgreSQL database run by our database provider, Neon, and the website is served by our hosting provider. Both act on our instructions and only process the data needed to run the service. Some of these providers may store data outside your country; where that happens, we rely on appropriate safeguards such as standard contractual clauses.</p>

<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
<p>We keep your email address until Encore launches and for as long as you stay subscribed to launch updates. If you ask us to remove it, we delete it from the waitlist promptly.</p>

<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>You can ask us to access, correct or delete your data, to restrict or object to how we use it, or to receive a copy of it. Email <a href={`mailto:${mail}`}>{mail}</a> from the address you signed up with and we will reply within one month. You also have the right to complain to your local data protection authority.</p>

<h2>Security</h2>
<p>Connections to this website and to our database are encrypted. Access to the waitlist is limited to the people who need it to run Encore.</p>

<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>If we change how we use your data, we will update this page and the date at the top. If the change is significant, we will tell you by email before it takes effect.</p>
